"stbench.mst — the SHARED Smalltalk benchmark workloads (ST_PLAN.md Sprint 8).

 Runs VERBATIM on both VMs:
   - MACVM:      cat stbench.mst macvm_driver.mst | its `macvm run`
   - MACDART-ST: stLoad'ed by run_macdart.dart, driven via stNew/stSend
 Pure compute, no printing, no timing — the drivers own that. Instance
 methods deliberately: every recursion/iteration is a real dynamic send
 (InstanceCall + inline cache) on both VMs, which is the thing being
 measured. run_macdart.dart carries a line-for-line native Dart mirror
 (DBench/DCell), so the same algorithms also run as ordinary Dart on the
 same MACDART VM — the ST-front-end tax measure."

Object subclass: STCell [
    | v |
    put: x [ v := x ]
    val [ ^v ]
]

Object subclass: STBench [
    fib: n [
        n < 2 ifTrue: [ ^n ].
        ^ (self fib: n - 1) + (self fib: n - 2)
    ]

    sumTo: n [
        | s i |
        s := 0. i := 1.
        [ i <= n ] whileTrue: [ s := s + i. i := i + 1 ].
        ^s
    ]

    blocks: n [
        | s b i |
        s := 0. b := [:x | x + 1]. i := 0.
        [ i < n ] whileTrue: [ s := s + (b value: i). i := i + 1 ].
        ^s
    ]

    alloc: n [
        | i c |
        i := 0.
        [ i < n ] whileTrue: [ c := STCell new. c put: i. i := i + 1 ].
        ^ c val
    ]
]
